# Orbit — channel authority (locked 24 Sep 2026)

Authority is trust that the film is about the thing it says, from the same person, every week. A polished title does not replace that.

## Picture matches the sentence

If the line names Jupiter, the shot is Jupiter. If the line names one probe, every appearance is that same craft. Put the measurement or the subject name on screen when the line names it.

Do not stand in a black hole, a desert, an ice canyon, a sci-fi tunnel, or a second spacecraft for a different subject. One world per film. A shot that is not the thing being said is wrong even if it looks polished.

## Orbit is the same character

Use the locked still `01_Orbit-Character/05_Seedance-References/orbit-seedance-reference-16x9-v01.png`. Matte orange floater, one large black curved visor, two cream eyes with dark pupils, stubby arms with dark three-finger hands, one antenna, one underside glow.

A melted face, a black void for a face, or a generic toy robot is not Orbit. Do not ship it. Do not use a rejected frame as the reference. Do not invent a new mascot per Short.

## The voice is there, and AI use is disclosed

Do not upload or schedule a film with a silent, stripped, or missing narration. Ben Orbit Narrator is the voice. YouTube’s use-of-AI / altered-or-synthetic disclosure is **yes** on every new upload.

## The weekly promise

One long a week. Three Shorts. One Short teases that week’s long. The other two promote films already up. Do not make a second long on a subject that already has a public long. Sources sit under the long. Talk to one person, and be the same Ben next week.

Do not schedule a long whose picture fails the match above.
